# SCHLAR — PROMPT 10: COMPLETE CRUD, DEMO DATA, VALIDATION & WORKFLOW RELIABILITY

## 1. YOUR MISSION

Continue developing the **existing SCHLAR school-management project**. Prompts 1–9 have already established the foundation, role workspaces, shared school modules, and cross-role integration.

Your mission now is to make every existing module genuinely usable through complete frontend interactions, realistic interconnected demo data, correct validation, safe record management, and dependable workflows.

**Do not create a new project. Do not redesign the application from scratch. Do not replace existing pages with generic dashboards or static mockups.**

Inspect the current project and its implementation first. Identify which features are complete, partially implemented, broken, or missing. Then improve the actual code.

The result must be a professional, responsive, user-friendly school-management demo that behaves consistently when a user creates, views, edits, searches, filters, updates, archives, or deletes records.

